    <!--
    *********************************************************************************

    And here is the overly elabortate pseudo-pathfinding procedure:

        Boss "protects" a corner by having a close proximatity to it but slow speed to get there,
        as there's no (or if there is, it is unaware to me) "transition enemyWithin" parameter I make do
        by having the corner "listen" to the boss when it is on top of it, to morph into a corner of the
        previous number. The boss uses the transition "noneExist" to then move onto the next corner.
        Unfortunately I don't know how well the boss well actually "order" them, it may require a repeat order
        if having one single order on an overarcing phase will not be active when the boss comes within range.


    *********************************************************************************
    -->


